<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil lowers Canada oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil lowers Canada oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it lowered the price it would pay for Edmonton light sweet crude oil by C$6.00/cubic metre or C$0.95/barrel, to C$218.00/cubic metre or C$34.66/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Other new prices were listed as follows: Cromer light sour C$211.00/cubic metre, or C$33.55/barrel Bow River at Hardisty C$178.00/cubic metre, or C$28.30/barrel Midale at Cromer C$186.00/cubic metre, or C$29.57/barrel ((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
